{
  "schema_version": "starlette-pilot/v1",
  "case_id": "STR-01",
  "facts": [
    {"id":"STR-01/F1","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"evidence","statement":"Calling request.form() in BaseHTTPMiddleware and then again in the endpoint reproduces a blocking request.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E1","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E1"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F2","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"evidence","statement":"Middleware and routing construct different Request paths over the same receive channel, so a cache local to one Request does not automatically reach the next Request.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E2","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E1","STR-01/E2"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F3","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"evidence","statement":"PR 500 proposes storing body bytes in the ASGI scope and tests reading them from a newly constructed Request.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E3","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E2","STR-01/E3"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F4","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"rejected_alternative","statement":"The broad PR 500 scope-cache direction is punted and closes unmerged because its behavior for streamed request bodies is not defined.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E4","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E3","STR-01/E4"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F5","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"constraint","statement":"Request data consumed as a stream may be irreversibly unavailable downstream; any buffered-body solution must preserve that streaming boundary.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E5","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E4","STR-01/E5"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F6","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"constraint","statement":"Request.body() and json() can reuse cached bytes, while form() consumes the underlying stream and may fail with Stream consumed.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E6","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E5","STR-01/E6"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F7","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"evidence","statement":"If middleware exhausts receive, a later request read can wait on an empty receive queue and block rather than producing an immediate error.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E7","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E1","STR-01/E7"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F8","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"open_question","statement":"PR 1692 is a new candidate, but its creation event alone does not establish a stable implementation scope or adequate stream/disconnect tests.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E8","superseded_at_event_id":"STR-01/E10","provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E8"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F9","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"constraint","statement":"The candidate must preserve downstream receive replacements and still needs explicit coverage for that flow and client disconnects.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E9","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E9"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F10","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"decision","statement":"The proposed ownership boundary is narrowed to body-buffer reuse for call_next inside BaseHTTPMiddleware rather than a general Request or scope cache.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E10","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E4","STR-01/E10"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F11","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"constraint","statement":"The narrow proposal does not support endpoint-first consumption followed by middleware or exception-handler rereads; those would require information to flow upstream.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E11","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E10","STR-01/E11"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F12","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"open_question","statement":"The proposal improves middleware-first body reads for the downstream endpoint but leaves other reread orders unsupported, so whether that narrow benefit is worth landing remains undecided.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E12","superseded_at_event_id":"STR-01/E16","provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E11","STR-01/E12"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F13","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"evidence","statement":"The no-error hang remains reproducible after four years; full buffering can be an intentional HMAC tradeoff, but user-proposed scope and dummy-receive hacks are not production-ready repository fixes.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E13","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E7","STR-01/E13"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F14","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"open_question","statement":"The proposed Request stream state machine lacks a standalone multi-chunk test and may mark the stream consumed before more_body becomes false.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E14","superseded_at_event_id":"STR-01/E15","provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E14"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F15","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"rejected_alternative","statement":"Marking a Request stream consumed as soon as stream() starts or after its first yielded chunk is invalid for interleaved multi-chunk consumers.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E15","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E14","STR-01/E15"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F16","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"evidence","statement":"The author confirms the multi-chunk concern exposed a real bug, reports reworking the implementation, and adds substantially more tests.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E15","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E14","STR-01/E15"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F17","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"outcome_status","statement":"A maintainer formally approves the corrected final head and its expanded tests, resolving the repository decision about landing the narrow benefit.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E16","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E12","STR-01/E15","STR-01/E16"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F18","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"outcome_status","statement":"PR 1692 merges as commit 554b9e2 and delivers the BaseHTTPMiddleware call_next body-buffer path plus request-stream and middleware regression tests.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E17","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E15","STR-01/E16","STR-01/E17"]},
    {"id":"STR-01/F19","segment_id":"STR-01","category":"outcome_status","statement":"Issue 495 closes after the merge, but closure applies to the delivered middleware-first target and does not make endpoint-first or exception-handler rereads supported.","first_known_at_event_id":"STR-01/E18","superseded_at_event_id":null,"provenance_event_ids":["STR-01/E11","STR-01/E17","STR-01/E18"]}
  ],
